**Paper**: Periodicity-aware deep learning for polymers (PerioGT), Nature Computational Science, 2025

**Core Contribution**: PerioGT introduces a unified SSL framework for polymers that explicitly incorporates periodicity priors through three mechanisms: (1) Periodicity Augmentation (PA) — a chemical knowledge-driven sampling module that generates equivalent fragments from the same polymer chain as contrastive positive pairs; (2) PolymerGraph — a modular graph augmentation strategy using virtual nodes to explicitly encode additional conditions (molecular weight, copolymer type, etc.) and physicochemical properties; (3) Periodicity Prompt-Guided Fine-Tuning (PGFT) — attention-based prompts that aggregate equivalent motifs from PA augmentations and inject them into initial node features.

**Key Results**: SOTA on all 16 downstream tasks, including Tg (RMSE 30.8, the benchmark in our TopicState). Wet-lab validation achieved 83% screening success rate for antimicrobial polymers, identifying two leads with MIC=8 μg/ml against MRSA.

**TopicState Relevance**: This is the current SOTA on Tg and directly validates the "Self-Supervised Pretraining" hypothesis — multimer-based contrastive learning with periodicity priors substantially outperforms monomer-only SSL approaches. It provides concrete implementation details for periodicity-aware pre-training that can be studied, adapted, or improved upon.

