ED — simple MPNN + PA contrastive pre-training alone is insufficient (PerioGT-Lite=52.92 mean, PCR-v2=52.24 best variant). The co-design must include a mechanism for USING periodicity knowledge, not just learning it. However, prompt conditioning (PCFT) and feature injection (BlochSpec) both failed to provide this mechanism. The co-design must change HOW information flows during MP, not add conditioning/features afterward.", "H3 (Periodicity-Aware Pre-training): EXHAUSTED — PA contrastive pre-training provides variance reduction but NOT mean improvement. Monomer-trimer pairs are easy positives (cos_sim 0.94-0.97). PCFT confirmed monomer encoder produces degenerate representations (cos_sim=0.963). The periodicity prior must flow through MP channels, not be appended as conditioning or features.", "H4 (Message-Passing Mechanism Gap — REVISED from Representation-Usage Gap): The 50→30 gap is not just a representation-usage gap — it is specifically a MESSAGE-PASSING MECHANISM gap. Adding information AFTER message passing (graph-level features, prediction-head conditioning) is redundant or degenerate (BlochSpec, PCFT). Adding information FROM degenerate sources (monomer-level prompts) is useless (PCFT cos_sim=0.963). The gap requires changing HOW periodicity flows during message passing — periodicity must travel through the SAME computational channels as atomic features, not be appended separately.", "H5 (Architecture-Periodicity Matching — REVISED): Periodicity encoding must be injected at NODE level during message passing, not at graph level after MP. For GIN, this means RU virtual nodes that aggregate intra-RU structure and broadcast inter-RU coupling during MP (PolymerBipartite). For Chemprop, this means directed bond-level messages on periodic edges. Architecture-periodicity matching = periodicity features must flow through the same channels as atomic features, not be appended as separate conditioning.", "H6 (Monomer Encoder Degeneracy — VALIDATED): Monomer-level GIN encoders produce near-degenerate representations regardless of pre-training (PCFT cos_sim=0.963, consistent with PCR-v2 cos_sim 0.94-0.97). Periodicity is an inter-RU phenomenon — it lives in the coupling between repeat units, not within a single unit. Any solution must encode inter-RU coupling, not rely on monomer-level representations. Critical diagnostic: RU virtual node cos_sim must be <0.90 (discriminative), not >0.95 (degenerate like monomer).", "H7 (Feature Injection Redundancy — VALIDATED): Graph-level feature injection is redundant with message passing on sufficiently large graphs (BlochSpec: random features match real features, unweighted matches weighted). The GNN on trimer already captures structural information that spectral features encode. The 50→30 gap requires changing HOW information flows through the model, not WHAT information is appended at the end. Correlation ≠ usefulness: features with r=-0.64 target correlation can be redundant with existing model capacity.", "H8 (Message-Passing Mechanism Change — NEW, HIGH PRIORITY): The only remaining path to bridge the 50→30 gap is to change the message passing mechanism itself. Three candidates: (a) PolymerBipartite — node-level periodicity injection via RU virtual nodes during MP (adapts LSR-MP\'s validated bipartite paradigm); (b) Chemprop-Polymer — directed bond-level messages on periodic edges; (c) Equivariant MP with periodicity-conditioned attention. All three change HOW the model processes periodicity, not WHAT information it receives. Mandatory diagnostics: measure RU virtual node pairwise cos_sim (<0.90 required), include random feature controls, verify improvements come from mechanism change not parameter count."]', 'daily_journal': [{'day': 2, 'journal': "Day 2 Journal — Polymer Deep Learning Research\n\n**Learning**: Read JEPA (polymer SSL), GPS++ (molecular GPS+denoising), SPSE (path-based structural encoding better than RWSE for cycles).\n\n**Experiments**: (1) GPS-SPSE-Trimer: 54.41 RMSE — FAILED. Small-Graph Paradox: Transformer redundant on 30-60 node polymer trimers where MPNN already reaches all nodes. (2) JEPA pre-training collapsed (EMA+MSE → constant output). (3) Contrastive alternative: 50.77 — close but doesn't beat 50.19. Architecture alone and generic SSL alone both insufficient.\n\n**Internalization**: Architecture-SSL Co-Design Principle — simple MPNN + periodicity-aware contrastive is the only validated path. Three MetaMethod lessons: Small-Graph Paradox, SSL Collapse Prevention, Periodicity Priors Essential.\n\n**Ideas for Day 3**: PCR-v2 (in-training monomer-trimer contrastive), PerioGT-Lite (PA-based pre-training on PI1M), BlochPoly (Bloch theorem spectral decomposition)."}, {'day': 3, 'journal': "Day 3 Journal — Polymer Deep Learning Research\n\n**Learning**: Read Antoniuk et al. (periodic polymer graphs + MPNN, ~20% RMSE reduction) and MoCL (domain-aware contrastive). Key: periodic edges help Chemprop but hurt GIN (architecture-dependent); domain-aware augmentation needs hard positives.\n\n**Experiments**: (1) PCR-v2: FAILED — all variants worse than baseline (best 52.24 vs 51.34). Monomer-trimer pairs are easy positives (cos_sim 0.94-0.97). (2) PerioGT-Lite: FAILED — multi-seed shows no improvement (52.92±0.29 vs 52.49±1.25, p=0.53). Single-seed 49.83 was statistical fluctuation. Pre-training gives variance reduction only, not mean improvement.\n\n**Internalization**: Representation-Usage Gap (H4) — GIN learns periodicity but can't USE it. Architecture-Dependent Periodicity Encoding (H5). Simple GIN + contrastive paradigm EXHAUSTED.\n\n**Ideas for Day 4**: Chemprop-Polymer (architecture-periodicity matching), BlochSpec (computed Bloch band features as input — paradigm shift), PCFT (prompt-conditioned fine-tuning)."}, {'day': 4, 'journal': 'Day 4 Journal — Polymer Deep Learning Research\n\n**Learning**: Read SPSE (path encoding for cycles), GraphPrompt+ (prompt-guided GNN fine-tuning), LSR-MP (bipartite atom↔fragment MP for non-local interactions).\n\n**Experiments**: Both FAILED. (1) PCFT: 52.72±0.76 vs baseline 52.46±0.20 (p=0.64). Root cause: monomer encoder near-degenerate (cos_sim=0.963) — prompt carries zero discriminative info. (2) BlochSpec: 53.25±0.51 vs 51.71±0.33 (+1.54, WORSE). Root cause: graph-level spectral features redundant with MP; random features match real features.\n\n**Internalization**: THREE paradigms EXHAUSTED (contrastive, GIN innovation, graph-level feature injection — all 50-54 RMSE). HOW-vs-WHAT principle: gap requires changing MP mechanism, not adding info afterward. H4→"Message-Passing Mechanism Gap", H6/H7 validated, H8 new.\n\n**Ideas**: PolymerBipartite v2, Chemprop-Polymer v2, CEL (physics-first: compute conformational entropy from conformer landscape, correct with kernel ML — bypasses GNN paradigm entirely).'}]}, 'connections': {}}]}

